    media: qcom: camss: Add MSM8226 resources
    
    Describe two two-phase CSIPHYs, two CSID 4.1 instances, one ISPIF and one
    VFE using the existing legacy operations. Omit MSM8916's separate CAMSS
    AHB clock and use the MSM8226 VFE clock levels from 37.5 to 400 MHz.
    
    Keep the later integration change that scales the VFE AXI clock to
    266.67 MHz. Add vfe_axi to the clock-name matcher so its nonzero rate
    table is used. Other existing platforms have zero-only vfe_axi tables;
    the clock-level guard continues to exclude them.
    
    Refresh commit f8a7ccc43396 ("media: qcom: camss: Add MSM8226 resources"),
    rebased as 680a10f798d0, and AXI follow-up d1f8047db385. Adapt the entries
    to the current
    regulator_bulk_data format with a vdda supply and default zero load,
    preserving the integration's unspecified-load behavior. Do not copy a
    new load requirement from a different SoC.
    
    Both native ARM and ARM64 complete CAMSS components build with W=1 and
    incompatible function pointer warnings treated as errors. Clock,
    register and interrupt names agree with the binding. The vendor VFE 4.0
    uses the reused 4.1 operations in the existing integration; hardware
    acceptance on this media-next base remains open. Board and IOMMU support
    are separate dependencies.
    
    Original integration attribution credits Claude Opus 5.5
    <noreply@anthropic.com> as a co-author. This refresh and host qualification
    used OpenAI Codex assistance. Human review and DCO remain pending.

